1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:14,000
ATTACK WITH DETECTOR — same attack,
same autopilot, same network.

2
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Only the ground station changed.
No new sensor, no extra message.

3
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:04,000
It times each report against its
own arrival clock. Nothing else.

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Telemetry age at the GCS: 18 ms.
The detector stays quiet.

5
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
The adversary starts now.

6
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:08,000
STALE STATE — the alarm fires about
2 s after the attack begins.

7
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The age is shown live, in seconds,
and the track turns red.

8
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Telemetry age at the GCS: 14 s.
Exactly the same attack as before.

9
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:56,000
The detector does not stop it.
The state is just as stale: ~51 m.

10
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:16,000
What changed is that the operator
can now see it. That is the point.

11
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Still no failsafe, still no link
alarm — those monitors see nothing.

12
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Silent state staleness,
no longer silent.
